The change fixes the three reported cases and the email index is now per organization. I checked every API route's store call against its org scoping. The only ID-only lookups that remain (`CustomerByID`, `InvoiceByID`, `EventByID`, `Delivery`, `DeleteWebhookEndpoint`) are reached from the webhook sender, the admin tool, or the payments code, not from an API handler. Payment, subscription, and usage paths were also checked. Nothing in the API lets a caller reach another organization's data.

The new tests cover the 404 equivalence, the no-side-effect checks, and the per-org email behavior. On the original code, the email test and the invoice-lines, create-with-foreign-customer, and endpoint-delete tests would fail, which matches the definition of done.

